You'd need to acquire 101 points of digging effort in one go. Each
turn of digging is a base d5+9 (so 14 at best), plus your to-hit bonus
from strength and dexterity (+14 is the best reasonably feasible),
plus the enchantment of the digging implement (+7, let's say), minus
any erosion penalty, plus any increase damage bonus from rings (let's
say +7 again). That for a total of 42; double if you're a dwarf, so
84.  Still not enough; so you'd have to have really remarkable kit to
be able to dig through a wall in one turn without using a wand or a
spell.

